CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: Holds for the claimed seam and workload slice: real C4 multilingual docs, 20,000 measured docs, 9,044 model-identical NFKC-twin pairs, 45.2% pair-formable prevalence, 34.6% MinHash survival at T=0.8 with 95% CI [33.6%,35.6%]. Gaps: not a full-corpus web-scale run, not tied to one loaded tokenizer.json, and downstream memorization/eval-contamination effect is inferred from hidden duplicate exposure rather than trained-model measurement.
RATIONALE: v001. This is not systems mechanism novelty; the revision correctly frames it as empirical measurement of the IIR §2.2 equivalence-class normalization mismatch at the dedup × tokenizer seam. OSS search found production dedup tools that implement nearby MinHash/text normalization pipelines but do not implement model-tokenizer normalizer alignment: datatrove uses lowercase + NFD in simplify_text, and text-dedup uses lower + regex tokenization. Inference systems requested for comparison (vLLM/SGLang/LMCache/FlashInfer/TensorRT-LLM) are serving/cache/kernel stacks, not training-data dedup systems, and I found no overlap implementing this mechanism. The contribution is therefore a systems insight/measurement, not integration-only glue. The artifact is reproducible enough for this claim: EXP-0069 reports 95.1% residual FN on real C4 multilingual and 34.6% production MinHash survival; EXP-0070 adds bootstrap CIs and driver concentration, with fullwidth_ascii top-1 77.4% but other_compat 19.0% and de/fr clearing ~94.6% without fullwidth ASCII, so the result is not only a single Unicode class artifact.
